<title>USA: USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</title>
<headline>USDA gross cutout hide and offal value.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The hide and offal value from a typical slaughter steer for Friday was estimated at 9.32 per cwt live, unchanged when compared with Thursday's value. - USDA</p>
<p>FOB CENTRAL U.S. TODAY'S CALCULATIONS FOR BY-PRODUCT VALUE</p>
<p>(STEER) -			   Lbs   Price  Change   Value</p>
<p>Steer hide, butt brand	 5.13   89.50    -	 5.89</p>
<p>Tallow, edible		   1.20   18.75   -1.00    0.23</p>
<p>Tallow, packer bleachable    4.50   15.75    -	 0.71</p>
<p>Tongues, Swiss #1 Wht 0-3%   0.26  162.00    -	 0.42</p>
<p>Cheek meat, trmd		 0.32   65.00   -2.00    0.21</p>
<p>Head meat			  0.13   60.00    -	 0.08</p>
<p>Oxtail, selected		 0.16  160.00   -1.00    0.26</p>
<p>Hearts, reg, bone out	  0.38   25.25    -	 0.10</p>
<p>Lips, unscalded		  0.11   80.00    -	 0.09</p>
<p>Livers, slcted, gall off     0.96   39.00    -	 0.37</p>
<p>Tripe, scalded edible	  0.65   21.00    -	 0.14</p>
<p>Tripe, honeycomb bleached    0.15   38.00   -3.00    0.06</p>
<p>Lungs, inedible		  0.47    4.60    -	 0.02</p>
<p>Melts				0.14    6.25    -	 0.01</p>
<p>Meat bone ml, 50% blk/ton    3.70  295.00    0.50    0.55</p>
<p>Blood meal, 85% blk/ton	0.60  600.00    -	 0.18</p>
<p>TOTAL :			   18.86			  9.32</p>
<p>The average value of hide and offal for the five days ending Friday, April 11, 1997 was estimated at 9.36 per cwt., down -0.12 from last week and up 1.09 from last year. ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
